## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical CBA for a local-first search feature, balancing storage, CPU, and privacy.

## Key Concepts
- On-device indexing
- Delta sync costs
- Privacy/compliance
- Update cadence and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
function indexRepo(files) {
  // naive tokenization
  const index = {};
  for (const f of files) {
    const tokens = f.content.split(/\\W+/).filter(Boolean);
    tokens.forEach(t => (index[t] ||= []).push(f.path));
  }
  return index;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure user time saved and energy impact to validate the break-even?
- How would you design for monorepos and very large repos with incremental indexing?

## Why This Is Asked

Balances privacy, regulatory needs, and system load by moving KYC attestation on-device.

### Key Concepts

- On-device cryptography and attestation
- Data minimization and privacy
- Key management and rotation
- Compliance and auditability

### Code Example

```javascript
async function signAttestation(privateKey, payload) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const data = enc.encode(JSON.stringify(payload));
  const sig = await crypto.subtle.sign({name: 'ECDSA', hash: 'SHA-256'}, privateKey, data);
  return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(sig)));
}
```

### Follow-up Questions

- How to handle key compromise and revocation?
- What metrics drive break-even and rollout schedule?
- How to prevent replay attacks and ensure forward secrecy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a feature into a practical 12‑month CBA with edge constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference costs (latency, energy, memory)
- Privacy and data minimization
- Cloud review costs vs offline results
- Rollout strategy and drift/maintenance costs
- Break-even horizon selection

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateCBA(modelSizeMB, perInferenceJ, inferencesPerMonth, cloudCostPerEvent) {
  const energyKJ = perInferenceJ * inferencesPerMonth;
  const yearlyEnergyCost = (energyKJ / 1000) * 0.9;
  const cloudYear = cloudCostPerEvent * inferencesPerMonth * 12;
  const total = modelSizeMB + yearlyEnergyCost + cloudYear;
  return total;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify drift/maintenance costs and retraining cadence?
- How would latency targets influence model size vs accuracy trade-offs?
- What metrics would you track to decide go/no-go?

## Why This Question Is Asked
This evaluates cost modeling for federated, multi-app ML with privacy constraints—a realistic production use case at companies like Google (Gboard), Apple, and Meta. It tests ability to identify cost drivers, trade-offs between privacy and accuracy, and phased rollout planning under regulatory constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning with secure aggregation and differential privacy
- Cross-app governance, regional data locality (GDPR, CCPA, PIPL)
- Bandwidth, energy, and memory budgeting on mobile devices
- Model drift detection, concept drift, and maintenance pipelines
- Phased regional rollout with go/no-go gates

## Code Example
```javascript
function calculateCBAPhase(devices, roundsPerDay, daysPerMonth, payloadKB, costPerGB) {
  const activeDevices = devices * 0.30;
  const monthlyUplinkGB = activeDevices * roundsPerDay * daysPerMonth * payloadKB / 1024 / 1024;
  const monthlyCost = monthlyUplinkGB * costPerGB;
  return {
    devices, activeDevices, monthlyUplinkGB, monthlyCost,
    breakEvenUsers: monthlyCost / 0.10
  };
}

function rolloutPhase(phase, criteria) {
  return {
    phase,
    go: criteria.every(c => c.passed),
    gates: criteria
  };
}
```

